#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:214 b9c6c0eb48fc4d1f934550acf2a00ad8
msgid "A-8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:216 17b8e435c315447499dd8532a4dff0ae
msgid ""
"I sized the trace record at 32 bytes in the header comment and in the "
"case that pins its size. It is 36: four bytes of timestamp, **seven** "
"floats, two bytes of state. The wrong number came from counting six "
"floats in a list of seven, and it had already been copied into two files "
"before the assertion noticed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:219 2de22276c3244f37970bc00e24ecf87d
msgid ""
"The assertion itself, `EXPECT_EQ(sizeof(TraceSample), 32U)`, which "
"reported 36 on its first run. Nothing else would have: a struct that is "
"four bytes larger than documented changes how many periods fit in 2 KiB, "
"and no other case cares."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:222 c3a0a0f6ced449f9be2e6cafcff4694e
msgid ""
"Two comments and one test constant. Which is the point of pinning a size "
"at all -- the claim \"2 KiB holds N periods\" is now arithmetic nobody "
"has to remember."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:226 9ba9b7514d1442ffa907e4eca48e62a2
msgid "F-6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:228 03814e8da4944da9b0cc06a6c8e3f7b4
msgid ""
"`foc_bridge_get_setup` copied seventeen fields of the setup and silently "
"dropped the six that had been appended to `foc_motor_setup_t` over three "
"waves: `observer`, `inject_v`, `inject_hz`, `blend_start_rad_s`, "
"`blend_end_rad_s`, `handover_lpf_hz`. `Motor.setup()` -- the first place "
"a support engineer looks -- therefore reported the *defaults* for exactly"
" the fields that choose the observer, while `status()[\"observer\"]` "
"reported the truth from the live object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:233 9685445090ed42789f1a669e2fd11bc7
msgid ""
"Building the first golden window: the readback said `observer=BACK_EMF, "
"inject_v=0` while `status()` said `HFI` for the same motor. No test "
"caught it because every readback case asserted only pre-append fields -- "
"the test asked whether the fields it knew about came back, never whether "
"the struct came back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:236 a38adc6382664b10a0b4523ebab317e8
msgid ""
"One function, plus a case that sets every field and demands all of them "
"back, so the next appended field is caught in the same place it is added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:239 26e9bf2db6974541be67a822d1466954
msgid "F-7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:241 48f8e989afb84cf98c50bc8623e43268
msgid ""
"Selecting the injection observer through `Motor` applied **no carrier at "
"all**, on any axis whose HAL supplies an angle. `tick()` took the sensor "
"branch, so the observer was never stepped; an observer that is never "
"stepped never advances its carrier phase, and a carrier frozen at phase 0"
" sits at a zero crossing, so `injection_ab()` returned exactly 0.0 V. The"
" mode was admitted, reported as ``HFI`` by `status()`, and inert -- every"
" surface agreed with the caller except the inverter. The C host path "
"always supplies an angle (`read_angle_mech_rad` is required by the HAL "
"contract), so this was the whole Python face, not an edge case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:247 68ac184da9364c2eab45a806fcd4631c
msgid ""
"Trying to record a golden window for the injection path: the duty swing "
"over 3000 periods was 0.00000 while `status()[\"observer\"]` said `HFI`. "
"Instrumentation, not inference, then narrowed it: the "
"`SwitchableObserver` standalone injects ±9.56 V (so the slot forwards), "
"the composed `HfiObserver::update` **never printed** (so it was never "
"called), and `injection_ab()` read 0 because `phase_applied_` had never "
"moved. No existing case caught it because every ABI case asserted "
"admission and the reported mode, and the W7-c SIL work drove "
"`HfiObserver` directly -- the composed path was covered by nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:253 7537d97107b34ffbbbecd22f276c1432
msgid ""
"Two gates in `tick()`, plus one case that asserts the carrier reaches the"
" inverter on a sensored axis and one that keeps asserting it on a "
"sensorless one. The observer is now stepped whenever it injects "
"(``speed_from_observer || injecting_now()``), and the carrier is added on"
" the same condition. The sensor keeps the commutation angle and the "
"published speed, so an encoder rig gets a hybrid drive rather than losing"
" its angle to a carrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:259 2fc3bb0afbc64df8b02de087caf5fc3b
msgid "F-7a"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:261 5ffcde21730d48a0a383e94039359b04
msgid ""
"The first fix attempt widened the carrier gate alone "
"(``speed_from_observer || injecting_now()``) and the case passed -- which"
" proved nothing, because the observer's phase starts at 0 and the "
"injection was zero either way. Reverting the fix left the case green: an "
"unfalsifiable test standing in for a fixed defect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:264 13b1cffef23e499db8a2f811c7258ac8
msgid ""
"Reverting the fix and re-running it. The criterion has to be able to go "
"red; the way to know is to make it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:265 8b7e305f6d044415aa8f6da65c55a889
msgid ""
"The second attempt. Then the two halves were shown to be independently "
"load-bearing: reverting the *step* gate alone (carrier gate left open) "
"gives a swing of 0.0000, and reverting the *carrier* gate alone gives "
"0.0000 as well. Both were needed, and neither was detectable from the "
"diff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:269 e908117f87b344b09630ff400e77a246
msgid "F-7b"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:271 0c111a4c846e4837bee1525ecf23cbd4
msgid ""
"The second fix attempt refused the mode at `init()` when the observer "
"type could inject -- using ``has_injection_v<Observer>``, which is a "
"property of the **type**, not of the selected mode. Every motor whose "
"observer could switch modes was refused, and 38 cases went red. Narrowing"
" the probe to ``injecting()`` (the mode) brought it to 6, still the wrong"
" answer: the refusal was treating an inert carrier as correct by refusing"
" to run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:275 a014cdab9e6f490ba2896b0ce198d49f
msgid ""
"The test suite itself, in the same run. The trait answered \"can this "
"type ever inject\", the question was \"is this mode injecting now\", and "
"only the test count separated the two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:277 7ac258cc150d4d919386e622e377440e
msgid ""
"The refusal, removed. A mode that is admitted must run; refusing "
"admission is how a defect becomes a documented limitation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:280 90743edc030e426588d2025346a531e7
msgid "A-9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:282 95a2af9c0c5441479a3360dd6a98ae0c
msgid ""
"The probe that first measured F-7 ran with `pwm_freq_hz = 0` in the "
"setup, which drives the carrier phase increment to zero on its own. The "
"0.00000 it reported was therefore guaranteed before the defect was "
"consulted -- and the same rig, after the fix, still read 0.00000 at 6 kHz"
" and would have looked like a failed fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:285 c0a400856d134fb09bdf63eb93466dd3
msgid ""
"Sweeping the carrier rate against an explicit `pwm_freq_hz`: the same "
"code, one knob changed, went from 0.00000 at 1/2/4/5 kHz to "
"0.60/0.65/0.66/0.67. A probe is only worth its reading once it has been "
"shown able to produce a non-zero one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:288 769cf267082e40e89fd0aa544d17b731
msgid ""
"The F-7 verdict, re-measured. Pre-fix 0.00000 at all four rates with "
"`observer = HFI`; post-fix 0.45-0.67 across eight rate/PWM combinations. "
"Same window, one knob, both directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:292 2a824ba8f96849099c0db88105eb1048
msgid "F-8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:294 9dc47cb0d3ae4175b3d0178037108c42
msgid ""
"`benchmark/script/foc_sil_plant.py` added the **mechanical** acceleration"
" `torque / j` to `omega_e`, which is an **electrical** speed, and then "
"divided by the pole-pair count when reporting mechanical speed. Every "
"mechanical transient in the Python plant was therefore `pole_pairs` times"
" too slow -- measured **7.002x** at seven pole pairs on an open-loop "
"acceleration test against `T / J`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:298 0faf6dcf13cb473cbd94ac27ed47ef3d
msgid ""
"The analysis layer's analytic criterion, on its first run. The fitted "
"bandwidth of a speed step on the Python face read **17.78 rad/s against "
"the 250 rad/s the setup asked for**. Varying one knob at a time separated"
" the suspects: the fitted bandwidth scaled exactly as `1 / kt` and "
"exactly as `j`, which is the gain law behaving correctly on a plant that "
"was too slow to respond, not a gain law that was wrong. A two-line open-"
"loop test then produced the number 7.002."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:303 d5fa0581298b428487690c26899662e5
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Every mechanical quantity ever derived from that plant. The golden "
"ledger's `speed_step_100` settled in 0.2 s (the whole window) and now "
"settles in 0.0211 s; its \"overshoot\" was a 5.6 % *undershoot* of a loop"
" still crawling, and is now +0.005 %. The three windows were re-recorded,"
" and every figure that had been quoted from them replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:308 5c220367304743e991184efdb105a36b
msgid "F-9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:310 79121705d7fe4817b80de25399cfcb67
msgid ""
"The same plant integrated a fixed 50 us (`DT`) per `write_duty` call, "
"while `golden.py` ticks at 100 us. The model advanced half a period per "
"call, so simulated time ran at **half speed** -- an exact factor of two "
"on top of F-8's seven."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:313 84f83b8bf355458fb6913af659fb904a
msgid ""
"Reading the constant after F-8's factor of seven did not explain the "
"whole 14x: 250/7 = 35.7, and the measurement said 17.8. `grep DT` found "
"`50e-6` against the caller's `1e-4`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:315 b7d0a5e7417e43d8972d61ec2733068f
msgid ""
"The plant now takes `dt_s`, `golden.py` carries one `DT_S` that both the "
"loop and the plant use, and the two development scripts that already "
"ticked at 50 us are unaffected. Together F-8 and F-9 account for 14.05x, "
"and the corrected measurement is 243.57 rad/s against 250 (-2.57 %)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:319 bde19571d5634373bbdce241d4da760c
msgid "A-10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:321 233b783083134367a3bf68a0b03b33ea
msgid ""
"The ledger could not have found either defect, and it was not asked to: "
"it compares the Python plant against a recording *of the same Python "
"plant*. A self-referential baseline detects regressions and is silent "
"about initial errors, however long it is stared at."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:324 cbb95327df214a4fa8cd2690dd1941df
msgid ""
"The analysis layer's second opinion -- the gain law's analytic bandwidth "
"on one side, the C++ bench's independent plant on the other. Neither "
"shares a line of model code with the Python plant, and the disagreement "
"was 14x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:326 e33689658f774a7db4d64c4e5cbdc267
msgid ""
"The reason 1.3 was worth doing before more scenarios were added: a ledger"
" with one implementation can only say \"unchanged\", and \"unchanged\" is"
" how a wrong model becomes a specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:330 e15496c17d7d4da4ba937cff4a033d14
msgid "A-11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:332 f355d20acf6c40d791d70eca786c4408
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The absolute 10 % criterion was written into the plan, met at 9.15 %, and"
" looked like a passing gate. Scaling the speed loop's proportional gain "
"by 0.8 -- a 20 % error in the gain law the criterion exists to check -- "
"moved the reading to 225.31 rad/s, i.e. **-9.88 %, still inside the "
"band**. The estimator's own +9.15 % bias was the same size as the defect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:336 551bfb1113c24db08e5c2601805862a2
msgid ""
"Perturbing the thing the criterion is about, rather than trusting it "
"because it went green. A tolerance met by an estimator whose bias is "
"comparable to the effect has almost no discriminating power, and no "
"amount of reading the tolerance reveals that -- you have to break the "
"system and watch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:339 ea77502df6f140909de039080c9f0dc4
msgid ""
"A second criterion that cannot be hidden by the bias: request 125 and 250"
" rad/s and demand the measurements move by the same factor (measured "
"134.66 and 272.87 rad/s, ratio 2.026). It catches a loop that ignores the"
" request, not a scale error -- the frequency sweep that catches scale "
"errors is the next increment, and this row is why it is the next "
"increment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:345 745f4b26c3174bd4bfe17c009f31af57
msgid "A-12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:347 edef3ccf06314e81b9340fda9587f962
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The first version of the sweep found the -3 dB crossing by interpolating "
"in log-log space between 0.5 and 2 times the bandwidth, and reported "
"**180 rad/s for a loop whose answer is 235** -- a 28 % error, made "
"entirely of interpolation. Interpolating a first-order magnitude between "
"two points that far apart is not a straight line: reduced per point (wb ="
" w / sqrt(1/g^2 - 1)) the same four measurements give 236.4, 235.8, 236.4"
" and 238.3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:351 861c746bd8a048618dd14d53b40b8dc3
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Reducing every measured point individually instead of trusting the "
"interpolant. The four values agreeing to 1 % is what proved the loop is "
"first-order at the Python face and the error was the arithmetic between "
"the points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:353 e4d3ec0be4d248578f18a7be652af1c0
msgid ""
"The -3 dB definition: the sweep now bisects, which assumes nothing about "
"shape. The C++ bench turns out *not* to be first-order (its per-point "
"equivalents fall 269.5 to 188.8), which the interpolation had been "
"hiding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:356 969ea1af1167421c89a5c913e49cb7c0
msgid "A-11b"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:358 ef5c10171f6540cfb1a492f47f676fc0
msgid ""
"A-11 said the frequency sweep would catch what the absolute step band "
"cannot, and left it as a claim about a future instrument. It is now "
"measured on the same defect: scaling the speed loop's proportional gain "
"by 0.8 moves the sweep's crossing from 234.91 to **210.79 rad/s (-15.68 "
"%, outside the 10 % band)** while the step fit moves from +9.15 % to "
"-9.88 %, still inside its own. Same defect, two instruments, one blind "
"and one not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:362 baa11d33871f4c59af7830feb5621130
msgid ""
"Running both criteria against the same perturbation, which is the only "
"way to know which one is carrying the claim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:364 f0d57080630046a9b1328285bf5105b6
msgid ""
"The sweep is now the criterion that carries it; the step response stays "
"because it says something different (how the servo behaves, not where its"
" corner is)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:368 8f2e0a5f077f4ab9a8c114f5591c0e0d
msgid "A-13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:370 f0eaac50f8714b63ac454511312cfc16
msgid ""
"The first Monte-Carlo criterion -- \"with `sigma = 0` the harness must "
"reproduce the nominal measurement bit for bit\" -- called one trial twice"
" and compared the two. It was green, and it could not fail: it never went"
" through the sampler, so the bug it exists to catch (a sampler that "
"perturbs by a hair when asked not to) was invisible to it. Drifting the "
"sampler to add 0.001 to sigma left the case green."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:374 da7b5125d7f94f9ca7423a0355e55b75
msgid ""
"Drifting every criterion and watching which ones stay green. Three of the"
" four drifted cases went red; this one did not, which is how the hole was"
" found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:376 7ef89fc150b341159f3eee10ab90975f
msgid ""
"The criterion now runs the *stream*, so `draw()` is in the path: the same"
" 0.001 drift produces 244.4909 against 244.4273 and the case fails. Third"
" instance of one family -- A-6 (\"a control that is never exercised\"), "
"A-11 (\"a band the defect fits inside\"), A-13 (\"a criterion that "
"bypasses the code it is about\"). The common cause is that a green test "
"is evidence of nothing until it has been made to go red."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:382 a8434aeea8ee47c8ba6fc1948c4cecab
msgid "A-14"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:384 b1635ccc9eb6451b866aca9e2b2f29a7
msgid ""
"The first version of the torque map's arithmetic case asserted that a "
"positive `id` *raises* the torque on an `ld < lq` machine. It lowers it: "
"the reluctance term is `1.5*pp*(ld-lq)*id*iq`, so the sign follows `ld - "
"lq` and the usual interior machine has `ld < lq`. The map was right and "
"the case was wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:387 766538096dc843f2829f36c144d1e803
msgid ""
"The case failing against arithmetic that was already correct, and the "
"analytic expression it was comparing with. Nothing in the map had to "
"change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:389 00534aeb4ff840b19db41175c630332c
msgid ""
"Two assertions, and one more reason the case states the expression "
"instead of quoting a number: a quoted number would have been edited to "
"match the wrong sign."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:393 37deac7396374c5cb388e38cb491551d
msgid "C-4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:395 18aa18cb21f84d8293a1af1b43158739
msgid ""
"The graded protection ladder had a case for the derating curve "
"(`derated_limit(T)`, a pure function) and a case for the trip, and "
"nothing in between: no case ever stepped the protector with a temperature"
" *inside* the band, and no case anywhere asserted `active_mask`, so the "
"enum-order ranking the header documents was unexercised too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:398 ca0847b9ad74457e991f9c6cfb68d619
msgid ""
"Writing the two cases the plan's own criterion named -- \"each rung has a"
" case, and an implementation that trips without derating must be red\" --"
" and then building exactly that wrong implementation: replacing "
"`t_trip_c` with `t_derate_start_c` in the over-temperature condition left"
" **seven of eight** protection cases green. Only the new ladder case "
"failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:402 38a3eb3f44d64cd9936bac41aee0f252
msgid ""
"Two cases, and the `todo` in the capability matrix's boundary column that"
" had been standing in for them is now a case name. The rule this row is "
"about: a capability with a curve test and a trip test can still have no "
"test of the thing it is for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:407 3e1564c8ad2a49d092c093887c3327bb
msgid "A-15"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:409 acba4fc1823445218c15d8193686f9f4
msgid ""
"Building the stiction rig I wrote a \"current source\" that nulled `diq` "
"**at the current the plant happened to have**. That is a free integrator,"
" not a source: it holds the current wherever the transient left it. The "
"case's own arithmetic caught it twice -- 37.85 rad/s against a promised "
"40.00 with the d current drifting, then 35.49 with the d current pinned, "
"because `iq` had settled at 0.90988 A against a 1.0 A setpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:413 408a0d2c580144599098ccb83f5120c1
msgid ""
"Printing what the plant actually ended with (`id 0.00700 iq 0.90988`) "
"instead of reasoning about the voltage. Two fixes were guesses at the "
"voltage; the third read the state and the answer was in the current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:415 54e5b0f560ad46e2a9335cf2c5b67cfd
msgid ""
"The source now feeds the **setpoints** with the d-q cross-coupling: "
"steady speed 39.997 against 40.000, `iq` 1.00000, torque 0.050000. The "
"lesson: regulating a derivative is not regulating a value, and a case "
"whose arithmetic is exact will say so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:420 1261c762b1ee4f79b9b1a82f835812b5
msgid "C-5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:422 e0d4902b869347fab8694078ab0813ed
msgid ""
"The first version of the breakaway case could not tell \"it started\" "
"from \"it is still being held\": the plant's stiction band was 0.5 rad/s "
"and the sequence's release threshold was also 0.5 rad/s, so the two "
"thresholds described the same speed and \"last torque at rest\" and "
"\"first torque moving\" printed the same number. Separately the handover "
"value carried 5.4 ms of ramp -- 2.7 mN*m -- because the rotor has to "
"accelerate to the release speed, which was larger than the quantity the "
"case was checking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:427 2c6bd26428614657840bc16eb18436af
msgid ""
"Printing both numbers and noticing they were identical, then asking what "
"each threshold means: the band is a numerical necessity at the zero "
"crossing, the release speed is a physical claim about motion. They must "
"differ by a decade, and the handover's lag must be stated rather than "
"absorbed by the tolerance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:430 b4cb7a241d76420e9a21ca4e446a221d
msgid ""
"The case now separates them (band 0.01, release 0.05 for the plant run) "
"and states the observation lag instead of hiding it: 1 mN*m of slack, "
"measured at 0.5 mN*m."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:434 820d4ca2c8a340f6adc7f924d77cc016
msgid "A-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:436 79db3651a7514078905a66db604d0075
msgid ""
"Editing the plan I located the 3.2 row with `line.startswith('| 3.2 |')`."
" That pattern also matched the **ROI audit table's** own `| 3.2 | 1.00 | "
"1.50 | 低估 |` row, which sits two hundred lines earlier, so the two new "
"rows landed inside the audit table and the real 3.2 row in the Phase 3 "
"table was never touched. The script printed \"3.2 closed\" and I believed"
" it; the plan still said the work was undone, and the user found it, not "
"me."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:440 1295f76244c54a8389b9faa192e91647
msgid ""
"Reading the artifact back instead of the tool's own success message. "
"`grep '^| 3.2'` on the finished file would have shown two rows in one "
"place and none in the other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:442 6847a8be137847dcb98ea59fedf8a54e
msgid ""
"The two rows moved to where they belong, the audit table's row restored, "
"and the plan now states the ordering policy it was silently applying. The"
" rule: **a tool's \"done\" is a claim about the tool, not about the "
"file** -- the same shape as A-4 (did not look before starting) and A-13 "
"(a criterion that bypassed its own subject), and the same fix: look at "
"the artifact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:448 cd7ad401c1d74f6e9cd1f4885ce3eabe
msgid "C-6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:450 e40437ee24c247f7ada0fb2960315237
msgid ""
"The criterion for \"a dead Hall sensor\" was written as \"somewhere two "
"bits change at once (6 -> 4), which is the trace of the missing sensor\"."
" Measurement says otherwise: the dead bit is **frozen**, so every "
"surviving transition still flips exactly one bit and the code walk "
"degenerates onto a smaller Gray cycle instead of breaking the rule. The "
"criterion would have gone red on a *correct* model, and the natural "
"repair for a red case is to change the model -- which would have broken a"
" model that was right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:455 5d5f0f70a5a34ca5ba2f865b16a581f1
msgid ""
"Measuring the model in a throwaway script before the first compile: the "
"flip counts for the stuck case read `[1,1,1,1]`, not `[1,2,...]`. "
"Reasoning would have kept the wrong signature, because \"a sensor is "
"missing so more than one thing must be wrong\" is a plausible-sounding "
"sentence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:458 30ede7d6e3584722a8907ba0fa77ac11
msgid ""
"The criterion, replaced by three facts measured instead: one 60-degree "
"illegal window per revolution (one sixth of the time), runs of 120 "
"degrees (the edge interval doubles), and three distinct legal codes left."
" Plus the assertion that adjacency **survives** -- the useful negative "
"result, since it says an adjacency check cannot be the fault detector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:463 d96bbd62101a4c578263dddc4f00db37
msgid "C-7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:465 70309e4755a345c9a1cabf3c73b170c5
msgid ""
"The quantisation case assumed the sector layout instead of reading it: it"
" took `theta = 0..60 deg` to be one sector. Sensors at 0/120/240 degrees "
"put their edges at 30/90/150/..., so **no** sector begins at zero; the "
"case straddled an edge and found two codes 59.96 degrees apart, then "
"reported it as a model error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:468 e87272f52b4849068cc11b5f8cbe50c0
msgid ""
"The case went red only after the sweep bug (A-17) was fixed; before that "
"every case failed on the count and the layout assumption stayed hidden "
"behind it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:470 05c9deb56d86450ba5576e34b571ce25
msgid ""
"The sector is now taken out of the sweep (the widest measured run), so "
"the case tests the sensor and not the arrangement. A model whose edges "
"are somewhere else now passes it, which is the point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:473 30fe47ef272a45b2879c05a399c29e62
msgid "A-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:475 313478e945424fdc8935b1411044693c
msgid ""
"The sweep that measures the sectors ran **two** revolutions: it computed "
"`samples = (2.0F * kTwoPiRad) / kStep`, and `kTwoPiRad` is already 2*pi, "
"so every count in the file was double six edge crossings instead of six, "
"twelve sectors instead of six, and a wrap-merge that had nothing to do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:478 8d296f6496774ef9adbb3897882a464a
msgid ""
"The very first assertion: `runs.size()` read 12 against an expected 6. "
"Five of the six cases in the file failed at once, and the sixth (no "
"illegal code anywhere) passed -- which localised it to the counting "
"rather than to the model, since the illegal-code sweep does not depend on"
" where the revolution ends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:481 3cb259a2446645bc81b60cee92c2097f
msgid ""
"One factor removed. The lesson recorded here is why the count was written"
" as an absolute number: a `>= 6` would have been satisfied by twelve and "
"the whole file would have read double forever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:484 b27a83fd2de742d2a0624e5fd754adcf
msgid "F-10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:486 fbef999516d44fc2ae3394b5bf167657
msgid ""
"`HallTracker` stored the first sample's timestamp as if it were an edge. "
"The rotor can be anywhere inside a sector when the first sample is taken,"
" so the interval from that sample to the first real edge is short by an "
"unknown amount -- and it became the reference every later interval was "
"judged against."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:489 36b3bd68f5dd473b89777d1551847e7f
msgid ""
"A perfectly healthy sensor set reported `State` on its second sector: 23 "
"samples of a 1280-sample run at 120 rad/s. The case that found it was the"
" one asserting `stale_fraction == 0` on a healthy run, which is the "
"negative half of the fault criterion and the only reason the startup path"
" was exercised at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:492 9b74d33876bd4a89952009f9d2f357d1
msgid "Intervals count only when both of their ends were edges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:494 cbb9512168664b38a9be07f684d6ec94
msgid "F-11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:496 a14e4e02251c442d82c8ac744f3dfe54
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The reference period was updated from any interval that arrived, "
"including one that was evidence of a fault. Two instances, opposite "
"directions: a **doubled** interval adopted as the new period let a dead "
"sensor become the tracker's idea of normal (36 % of a revolution "
"reporting `Ok` with an error up to 120 degrees), and a **short** one -- "
"six samples of a sliver-thin but genuine sector just after a fault "
"cleared (375 us against a 3.5 ms true period) -- poisoned the reference "
"so that every real interval afterwards looked late, i.e. `State` forever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:501 67f830c105a54a80b354ea7ad9b0223e
msgid ""
"Measuring the stuck-sensor case rather than assuming the fault channels "
"covered it, and tracing the recovery path sample by sample when the "
"status refused to return to `Ok` after the fault cleared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:503 30d6e328ad7e4e7fb12c6579334b9dda
msgid ""
"The interval test is now a two-sided band around the last period, and an "
"interval outside it is refused instead of adopted. Measured effect on the"
" dead-sensor run: the undetected fraction fell from 36 % to 8.4 % without"
" the false alarm on a healthy set changing at all (0 of 1280)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:507 1cd818ad781c4652ac2ef4949fea780f
msgid "F-12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:509 8799c03943164bbab74bb114ede98284
msgid ""
"Two things about a transition that crosses a stretch of illegal reads. "
"The crossing happened without being seen, yet the interval spanning it "
"was spent as a measurement; and the direction was taken from the shorter "
"arc of the code jump, which for a four-sector gap reads as two sectors "
"backwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:512 5a08475558e748d782c65951a060dae6
msgid ""
"The dead-sensor trace: the recovery edge was 119 degrees from the truth "
"while the status said `Ok`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:513 4a480542f4e64bad929d1100b46ffd9b
msgid ""
"A crossing during an illegal read is now marked unobserved and its "
"interval refused; and when the jump is too far for the short arc to be "
"meaningful, the direction falls back on the sign of the last known speed."
" Worst undetected error 120 -> 59 degrees on the low-stuck sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:517 e44506de5dbf4edf93239cea864fff97
msgid "F-13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:519 6e31c3adece74883b3b06672dc7b2b48
msgid ""
"The transition that carried a refused interval reported `Ok`. The verdict"
" was stored, and then the very sample that produced it returned `Ok` "
"unconditionally, so the next period said `State` and the one sample in "
"between -- the one holding the largest error of the run, 119 degrees -- "
"claimed to be a measurement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:522 9aa73b416b4a4815935b43ee9112432f
msgid ""
"Reading the trace rather than the aggregate: the worst undetected sample "
"sat exactly on a transition, which is where the status assignment and the"
" verdict were separated by one line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:524 42c74c50b9ce43d980015b2d9acb8a1d
msgid "The status of a transition now follows its own interval verdict."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:526 abf228757cdd4f798f2528a7caaf2e3e
msgid "C-8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:528 cc06076693da42788d021ad7775e8e79
msgid ""
"Three claims about `HallTracker` were wrong before any code shipped: that"
" the angle \"freezes\" during an illegal read (it free-runs and is "
"*clamped*, because the angle is a function of time); that the two fault "
"channels \"cover\" a dead sensor (they cover roughly two thirds of a "
"revolution); and that while `State` is up the angle is \"still good to a "
"few degrees\" (at 20000 rad/s^2 it is 42 degrees out, which is what makes"
" the flag load-bearing rather than decorative)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:533 c0ddd1913020428b8bcee1e6de891588
msgid ""
"Each one failed its own case on the first run, in the direction of the "
"case rather than of the code -- the signature of a claim written from "
"expectation instead of from the artefact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:535 f34b8a8ce5e447beaac4ce74dff657df
msgid ""
"The three cases now assert the measured behaviour and quote the numbers, "
"including the 42 degrees, which is the evidence for \"a loop on this "
"estimate must stop when the status says so\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:538 65f9b9dc23534a22a2b2d564a6b5b60f
msgid "A-18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:540 0d68fad9530b462b83b2f6c9e956d9ed
msgid ""
"The first rig that measured the dead band was scaled so that a 20 mrad "
"step demanded 1 N*m against a 3 A current limit: the loop saturated on "
"the first period and limit-cycled at 125 mrad, and the file measured that"
" instead of the friction. The module was never wrong; the instrument was."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:543 46816481997146c9a2d49f1d4b7a1789
msgid ""
"The trajectory print rather than the summary: `theta` swinging between "
"-26 and +125 mrad while the demanded torque sat on the clamp for most of "
"every cycle. Two symptoms pointed the same way -- the \"compensated\" run"
" did not settle either, and the ripple was 1.14 N*m when the term being "
"added was 0.010."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:546 91efbf3487b74a7690346a45b2068d56
msgid ""
"A velocity damping term (as any real position loop has) and a step that "
"stays inside the current limit. The dead band is set by the proportional "
"path at rest, where the damping term is zero, so the arithmetic being "
"checked did not change: 4.003 and 2.021 mrad against 4.0 and 2.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:550 f11d35ec87324562b3b17e9dd64e2adb
msgid "A-19"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:552 4cab51be2afa4e27b98dd088583121b2
msgid ""
"I predicted that an over-estimate past the breakaway would park the axis "
"`(coulomb - static)/kp` on the *wrong side* of the target. It does not: "
"the latch turns around as soon as the demand passes the term, so there is"
" no such equilibrium -- with the reference held at zero the axis simply "
"walks away, and the size of the walk is set by where the loop's own "
"demand finally balances the compensation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:556 2186628b134247afae5ce726186fa270
msgid ""
"Measuring it instead of deriving it: 114 mrad of excursion in the first "
"attempt and 5.625 mrad of net travel in the second, against a predicted 2"
" mrad in the wrong direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:558 8d17fa4e64ba4380836891557a917a32
msgid ""
"The case asserts the measured behaviour. The point survives and is "
"sharper than the prediction: an estimate above the breakaway is a motor, "
"and `validate()` can only catch the version of it that shows up in the "
"numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:561 613d50f565c04d20920f8818cbbd08d0
msgid "C-9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:563 41311842762f4e7ea3ad5ec4102367ad
msgid ""
"The first criterion for \"the residual drops\" was a single step's final "
"position. It is not reproducible: where inside the dead band the "
"trajectory happens to stop depends on the step size and the ringing, and "
"the same three mechanisms read 2.9, 1.1 and 0.24 mrad at 20, 20 and 200 "
"mrad steps -- a criterion that would have been \"fixed\" by choosing the "
"step that made it look right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:567 3b0d50401c344b7cb13aeb7072c3a369
msgid ""
"Measuring the same mechanism at three step sizes and getting three "
"answers, which is a property of the criterion and not of the mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:569 5de29896f550489c9580515da0b071d4
msgid ""
"The dead band itself is measured instead, by bisection on the reference "
"step: a threshold, not a snapshot of a trajectory, and it lands on the "
"arithmetic to four digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:572 ef84a03ba9c245b5ad326473b728d665
msgid "A-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:574 c1ad13a61c6042bb8cfa87d1d9a45e50
msgid ""
"The soft-limit case asserted the *ideal* invariant `v^2 <= 2*a*d` on the "
"plant's own state, and failed by 19 mm. The invariant is true of the "
"**command** from the instant the ceiling bites; the axis needs a delay "
"before the braking deceleration arrives, and during that delay it keeps "
"travelling at `v`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:577 f832de1acce6471f8f68ead45383c8b4
msgid ""
"The failure message did not say \"wrong criterion\", it said \"the shaped"
" run reached the wall\", and the trajectory showed the axis pinned at "
"maximum braking from the moment the ceiling appeared -- i.e. the loop was"
" doing everything it could."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:580 8d7608b710b342509572409c3334d813
msgid ""
"19 mm at 19.5 rad/s is 1 ms of travel, so the missing term was `v*dt`. "
"With it the ceiling becomes `v^2 <= 2*a*(d - v*dt)` and the axis stops "
"1.04 mm short. The case now runs all three: with the term, without it, "
"and with no shaper at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:584 c83ea167754b4f2f9e604e5844934d92
msgid "A-21"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:586 c110629a31144e4da5e09c4fc472ad68
msgid ""
"The first synchronisation measurement compared a *step* response and read"
" 58 mrad, which I attributed to the ramp lag `v*kd/kp`. It was not: a "
"step has no ramp, and what the number contained was the slave loop's own "
"ringing for the first 0.09 s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:589 1994968db12d463c9cfa7cbd8e4b9ac8
msgid ""
"Measuring a ramp instead -- and, separately, feeding the gear the ideal "
"ramp rather than the master's measured position -- separated the three "
"contributions: 25.6 mrad from the formula, +4 mrad from the master's own "
"tracking, and the rest from the transient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:592 8b204da1aea24f359f3b80904d69abd8
msgid ""
"The case now asserts the formula on an ideal ramp, its two scalings (`v` "
"and `kp`), and the residue the velocity feedforward leaves behind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:595 84b92c7afe3c470fb81b3b4f88ec7f63
msgid "C-10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:597 ad511d2c6be64d368311006eebcd29d8
msgid ""
"The criterion for the geared pair was \"sync error below 2 mrad\", "
"written before the mechanism was understood. A perfectly geared pair "
"cannot meet it: the standing lag is `v*kd/kp`, which is 25 mrad at the "
"configuration used. The criterion was wrong by an order of magnitude in "
"the direction that would have had me raise `kp` until the number passed "
"-- buying accuracy with the stability margin, and hiding the real lesson."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/foundation-log.rst:601 5fa6e3ead9b447e2b0da66c326599564
msgid ""
"The measurement landing 25.6 mrad against a 2 mrad criterion, and the "
